  "changes": [
    "Expose Array1 mutable prefix and bounded constructor entry points without ownership, initialization, or Clone requirements.",
    "Expose requested size/bounds independently of supplied buffer length for use_buffer=false; the input is ignored and nontrivial elements default-construct in new owned storage.",
    "Expose bounded mutable Array2 prefix construction, preserving row/column origins and native flat Array1 lower/upper bounds.",
    "Share checked inclusive extent and mutable prefix validation among existing and new Array1/Array2 entry points without changing resize algorithms."
  ],
  "probe_policy": "Native BufferItem records default/copy/destruction calls. Rust BufferItem has no Clone implementation and uses per-instance or constructor-injected Rc counters; there are no shared global test counters. The observed initialized objects and their destruction receipts are compared to the exact native rows.",
  "limitations": [
    "Native const-reference constructors can create arbitrary writable aliases; these entry points accept exclusive mutable slices and do not close the raw or const-cast aliasing domain.",
    "Rust buffer-length and negative-extent errors are checked extensions. Native out-of-bounds buffers or signed arithmetic overflow are not claimed.",
    "Use-buffer=false shares the Rust return lifetime with its input even though its runtime storage is independent; that conservative borrow-checker constraint is not native source-level parity.",
    "Rust Default corresponds to the probed nontrivial C++ default constructor. Primitive C++ uninitialized storage, arbitrary traits, allocation hooks/failures, and exception cleanup remain open.",
    "The unconstrained mutable view helpers can accept extra Rust types; this is not a claim that every equivalent bounded C++ const-reference instantiation accepts non-default-constructible elements.",
    "The safe from_shared copy-on-write extension is unchanged. No class or module is declared complete by these constructor-domain bindings.",
    "Original assertions are unchanged; supplemental constructor tests add no original legacy declaration credit."
  ],
